---
/**
 * How `validate` runs a pull request's commands: the base, only when it is on the default branch, installs with the
 * network and no script of the repository's, and its `node_modules` is kept as a snapshot; the head never installs
 * and never has the network, and runs only when every dependency file is the base's byte for byte.
 */
import Figure from "./Figure.astro"
---

<Figure label="The base installs, the head restores" minWidth={760}>
  <svg class="rv-svg" viewBox="0 0 920 300" role="img" aria-labelledby="bh-t">
    <title id="bh-t">Base: trusted check, install with network, snapshot, checks offline. Head: dependency files compared, snapshot restored, checks offline.</title>
    <defs>
      <marker id="bh-a" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="7" markerHeight="7" orient="auto-start-reverse"><path class="head" d="M0 0L10 5L0 10z"></path></marker>
    </defs>
    <text x="10" y="24" class="t-b">The base</text>
    <text x="90" y="24" class="t-xs t-dim">merged code of the default branch</text>
    {
      [
        ["trusted?", "on the default branch", "as the remote has it now", "box-2"],
        ["install", "the network shared;", "no script of the repo's", "danger"],
        ["snapshot", "node_modules saved", "before any check runs", "box"],
        ["its checks", "offline; each verdict", "kept by base and command", "core"],
      ].map(([name, a, b, cls], i) => (
        <g>
          <rect class={cls} x={10 + i * 226} y="38" width="200" height="82" rx="10"></rect>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="62" class="t-b t-sm">{name}</text>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="84" class="t-xs t-dim">{a}</text>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="102" class="t-xs t-dim">{b}</text>
          {i < 3 && <path class="line" d={`M${212 + i * 226} 79 H${234 + i * 226}`} marker-end="url(#bh-a)"></path>}
        </g>
      ))
    }
    <path class="line" d="M562 120 V146 H336 V176" stroke-dasharray="4 4" marker-end="url(#bh-a)"></path>
    <text x="350" y="140" class="t-xs t-accent">the snapshot, by its key</text>

    <text x="10" y="164" class="t-b">The head</text>
    <text x="90" y="164" class="t-xs t-dim">the pull request's code</text>
    {
      [
        ["same deps?", "every lockfile, package.json,", "manager config, patch", "box-2"],
        ["restore", "the base's snapshot,", "no network, no cache bound", "box"],
        ["its checks", "offline; a profile command", "only once it exited 0 on the base", "core"],
      ].map(([name, a, b, cls], i) => (
        <g>
          <rect class={cls} x={10 + i * 226} y="180" width="200" height="82" rx="10"></rect>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="204" class="t-b t-sm">{name}</text>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="226" class="t-xs t-dim">{a}</text>
          <text x={24 + i * 226} y="244" class="t-xs t-dim">{b}</text>
          {i < 2 && <path class="line" d={`M${212 + i * 226} 221 H${234 + i * 226}`} marker-end="url(#bh-a)"></path>}
        </g>
      ))
    }
    <rect class="box" x="688" y="180" width="222" height="82" rx="10" stroke-dasharray="4 4"></rect>
    <text x="702" y="204" class="t-sm t-b">otherwise nothing runs</text>
    <text x="702" y="226" class="t-xs t-dim">"dependencies changed: not</text>
    <text x="702" y="244" class="t-xs t-dim">validated locally (CI covers it)"</text>
    <text x="10" y="288" class="t-xs t-dim">A base off the default branch is refused: no install, no snapshot, no verdict kept. A head never installs.</text>
  </svg>
  <Fragment slot="caption">
    <strong>The network goes only to merged code.</strong> The one command that shares the host's network is the
    trusted base's install, run with the host's package manager by its absolute path and with the repository's
    install scripts off. The head reuses what that install made, offline, and only when nothing an install reads has
    changed.
  </Fragment>
</Figure>
